                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "This version isn't patched to 1.02, so it has a bug around the third \"level\" where going up an elevator to open a door to get further into the game is bugged.\r\n\r\nUnless you patch it it's a show stopper.\r\n\r\nI got the game in 2018 for $5 so I'm not upset, but there is no reason to buy this full price, especially with Interplay's death/dissolving.\r\n\r\nGame is also pretty mediocre. Interesting concept, but more frustrating to play than anything because the possession mechanic needs (on anything above \"easy\") to be from behind and some of the later characters (the big monster one especially) can be hard to possess because of it.\r\n\r\nWith refinement, it could've been good. But I think it's easily skippable.\r\n\r\n(Works on Linux, bar said bug. If you are able to patch it on Linux, let me know how you did it on the Steam forums as I'm curious. I had to play two levels on Windows before moving my save back to Linux to finish on a reverted 1.0/1.01 version after playing the \"bugged\" levels on patch 1.02, so saves work upgrading/downgrading, FYI.)",
